# Browser targets for this app.
#
# The problem this solves: Next.js compiles client bundles down to ES5 only
# when a browserslist config exists (see `getSupportedBrowsers` in
# next/dist/build/utils.js, which falls back to MODERN_BROWSERSLIST_TARGET —
# chrome 64 / firefox 67 / safari 12 — and the `jsc.target = 'es5'` fallback in
# next/dist/build/swc/options.js). Without this file the shipped JavaScript uses
# syntax that no i386-era engine can parse, so the bundle throws before React
# mounts and the page stays blank.
#
# It does *not* rewrite CSS. Verified by building and grepping the emitted
# stylesheet: :is()/:where() survive whatever is listed here. The :where() rules
# come from Tailwind's preflight and the typography plugin and are hard-coded in
# those plugins. The one :is() rule that was ours (the dark variant) is gone
# because tailwind.config.ts now uses darkMode: ["variant", ".dark &"], which
# prints a plain descendant selector instead.
#
# `>= 0.5%` and `not dead` are deliberately absent: they resolve to recent
# evergreen versions only, which is the opposite of the intent here.

# Oldest engines this app is expected to render in.
chrome >= 49
firefox >= 45
safari >= 10
edge >= 15
ie >= 11
